   "data": {
    "text": "Replay of 1 Sep 2021 Ida rain over Queens `nyc-queens-v0`\n\nModelled as planning model, not a forecast:\n\n* **Baseline:** `total_mm: 118, duration_h: 4, pattern: center_peaked`, rain over the whole study area, `sim_hours: 8`\n  * This matches the `Ida 1 Sep 2021 (LaGuardia gauge)` preset storm.\n* **Intervention test, one change at a time:** whole-area `drain_upgrade capacity_factor: 2.0` - i.e. double existing sewer capacity everywhere, not a local fix.\n\nNo river inflows in this area - `inflow_volume_m3: 0.0` in both runs.\n\n### 1. Baseline - what floods\n\nRun `r_48aae11b5d8514ed`, solver:\n\n* `buildings_flooded: 12531`\n* `buildings_flooded_severe: 4975`\n* `people_exposed: 45385`\n* `road_km_impassable: 92.198` km at 0.3 m threshold\n* `flooded_area_km2: 2.2384`\n* `max_depth_m: 4.521`\n* `peak_t_s: 12000` - ~3.3h after storm start\n* `drained_volume_m3: 1163496.2`, `infiltrated_volume_m3: 779262.6`, `stored_volume_end_m3: 729052.4`\n\nWidespread pluvial flooding with 92 km of roads impassable.\n\nNeighbourhood breakdown, same run:\n\n* **Elmhurst:** `area:Elmhurst:buildings_flooded: 3012`, `area:Elmhurst:people_exposed: 10775`, `area:Elmhurst:road_km_impassable: 27.055`, `area:Elmhurst:max_depth_m: 2.9`, `area:Elmhurst:flooded_area_km2: 0.6364`\n* **Jackson Heights:** `area:Jackson Heights:buildings_flooded: 2782`, `area:Jackson Heights:people_exposed: 9318`, `area:Jackson Heights:road_km_impassable: 15.922`, `area:Jackson Heights:max_depth_m: 2.279`, `area:Jackson Heights:flooded_area_km2: 0.4241`\n* **Corona:** `area:Corona:buildings_flooded: 2006`, `area:Corona:people_exposed: 14063`, `area:Corona:road_km_impassable: 25.635`, `area:Corona:max_depth_m: 4.52`, `area:Corona:flooded_area_km2: 0.5411`\n* **Woodside:** `area:Woodside:buildings_flooded: 1452`, `area:Woodside:people_exposed: 3429`, `area:Woodside:road_km_impassable: 9.529`, `area:Woodside:max_depth_m: 2.812`, `area:Woodside:flooded_area_km2: 0.1881`\n* **East Elmhurst:** `area:East Elmhurst:buildings_flooded: 935`, `area:East Elmhurst:people_exposed: 1933`, `area:East Elmhurst:road_km_impassable: 6.893`, `area:East Elmhurst:max_depth_m: 1.438`, `area:East Elmhurst:flooded_area_km2: 0.1526`\n\nIn this sample:\n\n* Most buildings flooded: Elmhurst > Jackson Heights > Corona > Woodside > East Elmhurst\n* Most people exposed: Corona > Elmhurst > Jackson Heights\n* Deepest local maxima: Corona 4.52 m - the study-area maximum - then Elmhurst 2.9 m, Woodside 2.812 m, Jackson Heights 2.279 m, East Elmhurst 1.438 m\n\nDepths >2-4 m are local low-pocket maxima, e.g. underpasses / depressed lots, not area-average water.\n\n### 2. Would doubling sewer capacity have helped?\n\nRun `r_e617927367a13c19`, same storm + sewers x2:\n\n* `buildings_flooded: 9113`\n* `buildings_flooded_severe: 1963`\n* `people_exposed: 21324`\n* `road_km_impassable: 44.154`\n* `flooded_area_km2: 1.0691`\n* `max_depth_m: 2.306`\n* `drained_volume_m3: 1859186.1`\n\nDifference alt - base:\n\n* `buildings_flooded: -3418.0` : -27% total\n* `buildings_flooded_severe: -3012.0` : -61% severe\n* `people_exposed: -24061.0` : -53%\n* `road_km_impassable: -48.044` : -52%\n* `flooded_area_km2: -1.1693` : -52%\n* `max_depth_m: -2.215`\n* `drained_volume_m3: +695689.9`\n\nYes - substantially:\n\nDoubling area-wide capacity drains ~0.70M m3 more, halves flooded area, road-impassable length and people exposed, and cuts severe buildings by ~3,000 and maximum depth from 4.52 m to 2.31 m.\n\nIt does not prevent Ida-scale flooding: >9,100 buildings still flooded, 1,963 severely, 44 km roads impassable and 21,324 people exposed remain. For this intensity, sewers alone are insufficient - residual ponding would need complementary storage / green / overland flow-path measures.\n"
   }
